  "term": "activity record",
  "definition": "An activity record is a log used to assess how much time a person spends in different activities over a set period, such as 24 hours. In this source, a 24-hour physical activity record was used to measure preschool children’s sedentary time, screen time, indoor play, outdoor play, and time spent going out.",
